Ticket #4471 merged 412 date reports and was marked known, as one parser bug: the shared parser reads the month first, and these tenants write the day first.

That is only the larger cause. `causeOf` splits the same reports into two. A form on `booking-v3` tells the person to type `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the date the tenant's way. That is `hint`, a different bug, filed in #4471 with no ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Known was the wrong close. One ticket held two problems.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is the count. `parser` is the cause most of these reports share, so it is the cause of #4471. `hint` is the rest. Five reports inside `parser` were read as a one-day move. They stay in that count. The desk notes them. They are not a third cause.

## Tickets

One ticket per problem, in this repo:

- `parser` — the month-first parser on a day-first tenant. The report count is the `parser` row above.
- `hint` — `booking-v3` shows `MM/DD/YYYY` while the tenant's locale writes the day first, and the report came in through the form. The report count is the `hint` row above.

